# The Mountains are sacrificed as a cost (CR 118.9, 601.2h), and a tapped Mountain can be sacrificed: Bot1 taps both for
# {R}{R} first, then casts Fireblast for its alternative cost. The mana made stays in the pool (it is not spent, the
# alternative cost has no mana), so both Mountains are gone, Bot2 takes four, and {R}{R} is still there to use.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mountain
Fireblast
Mountain x4
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fireblast.Cast(Bot2; Ability: Sacrifice)
Bot1.Choose(Mountain; Mountain)
? Bot1.Mana = {R}{R}

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 16
Bot1.Graveyard = Fireblast; Mountain; Mountain
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 0
